%N A038749 Number of equivalence classes under rotations and reflections of n-step self-avoiding walks on the cubic lattice that use all three coordinate axes and have exactly one pair of nonconsecutive vertices adjacent in the lattice.
%C A038749 In the notation of Nemirovsky et al. (1992), a(n), the n-th term of this sequence is p_{n,m}^{(l)} with m=1 and l=3. These numbers are given in Table II (p. 1093) in the paper. This sequence can be used for the calculation of sequence A047057 via Eq. (5) in the paper by Nemirovsky et al. (1992). (Note that, by equations (7b) in the paper, p_{n,m=1}^{(1)} = 0 for all n >= 1. Also, p_{n,m=1}^{(2)} = A038747(n) for n >= 1.) - _Petros Hadjicostas_, Jan 04 2019
%C A038749 From _Carlo Corti_, Aug 09 2026: (Start)
%C A038749 The previous name was "Coefficients arising in the enumeration of configurations of linear chains."
%C A038749 The full 48-element cubic point group of signed coordinate permutations acts on the ordered vertex sequence. Path reversal is not included in the equivalence relation.
%C A038749 The terms a(20)-a(24) were obtained by exhaustive cubic-orbit enumeration; a(25)-a(27) were extracted exactly from published fixed-first-step contact-polynomial coefficients and A038747. (End)
%H A038749 Carlo Corti, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21859588">A038749: Exact cubic-lattice one-contact enumeration</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A038749 A. M. Nemirovsky, K. F. Freed, T. Ishinabe, and J. F. Douglas, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01049010">Marriage of exact enumeration and 1/d expansion methods: lattice model of dilute polymers</a>, J. Statist. Phys., 67 (1992), 1083-1108; see Eq. 5 (p. 1090) and Eq. 7b (p. 1093).
%F A038749 a(n) = (A047057(n) - 24*A038747(n))/48 = ([x]Z_{n+1}(x) - 4*A038747(n))/8 for n >= 1, where Z_N(x) = Sum_w x^m(w), w ranges over N-monomer cubic-lattice self-avoiding walks with one prescribed first step, m(w) is the number of nonconsecutive nearest-neighbor contacts, and [x] denotes extraction of the coefficient of x. - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 09 2026
%e A038749 a(4) = 2. Representatives of the two equivalence classes are the step words +x,+y,-x,+z and +x,+y,+z,-y. Their unique nonconsecutive nearest-neighbor contacts are {v_0,v_3} and {v_1,v_4}, respectively. - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 09 2026
%Y A038749 Cf. A033155, A038747, A038748, A047057.
%K A038749 nonn,walk,changed
%O A038749 1,4
%A A038749 _N. J. A. Sloane_, May 02 2000
%E A038749 The first three 0's in the sequence were added by _Petros Hadjicostas_, Jan 04 2019 to make it agree with Table II (p. 1093) and Eq. (5) (p. 1090) in the paper by Nemirovsky et al. (1992).
